  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through next Monday)\nIssued at 1253 PM CDT Tue Oct 27 2026\n\nModels remain in good agreement with having a wet Thursday \nevening/Friday morning. Moisture from Tropical Storm Vance over the \neastern Pacific will be pulled northward with an upper shortwave \ntrough and will track over West Texas. Heavy rainfall continues to \nbe the main hazard expected with this next system as PWATs increase \nto around/just over 1.5 inches. Current forecast storm total QPF \nsits a 1.5-2.5 inches. Some areas may see more rain than this, \nothers possibly less. No flood watches are currently planned, though \nsome localized flooding will be possible. We should see rainfall \nexit the region by Saturday morning and, for a short period, be \nreplaced with upper ridging. Another storm system looks to be on tap \nby late Sunday into early next week. While the potential for \nrainfall does exist, there will also be some risk for dry slotting.",
